  "rfc": "RFC-257",
  "date": "2026-10-01",
  "reason": "Join planning follows Java 4.14.2.0 (RFC-257). PartitionSelectRule places a predicate spanning a bipartition in the lower, so join chains plan as right-deep correlated FlatMaps. SelectExpression merges comparisons on one value into one range, as Java's partitionPredicates does; partitioning splits it back per quantifier so a selective part still binds at its own leg. EXISTS bodies keep their WHERE below FirstOrDefault. A FLOAT column compared with a DOUBLE literal is promote(e AS DOUBLE), which select subsumption does not sarg, exactly as Java plans it: 60 scenarios lose an IDX_E equality probe for that reason. fc_0000000346_q0_p0..p2 are retired: they became the same (feature vector, plan shape) point as fc_0000000204_q2_p0..p2. The frozen rows are unchanged.",
